[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-silhouette@4da5046883246533fd9d015a70e87c1f10e51840/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#e8b99c]What it is[/color][/b][/size]

Without a distributor, every woman in the Commonwealth shares one body and every man another. Silhouette gives each of them a body the first time you meet them, keeps it for the rest of the save, and never re-rolls someone you have already met. It follows OBody NG's design, config keys, priority and API names, and it works through LooksMenu's own BodyGen, so the bodies are LooksMenu's and stay in your save.

[b]It measures your install instead of assuming it.[/b]
[list]
[*]A preset whose sliders your body's [font=Courier New].tri[/font] does not have would do nothing, so it is left out.
[*]If your base body was not built zeroed, Silhouette names the exact preset it was built from and the zeroed one to rebuild with, instead of stacking every NPC on top of it.
[*]Every body it writes is rebuilt the way LooksMenu builds it and checked to land on its preset.
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#e8b99c]Who gets which body[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Everyone: Silhouette's own pool.[/b] 41 bodies per sex, 82 in all, generated and measured rather than hand-picked, so no two look alike. 18 Plain, 17 Rough (very fat, very flat, frail, disproportioned) and 6 Fine, drawn at 70 / 22 / 8 %. The pickers also offer the stock CBBE and BodyTalk presets; those are never random. The generator adds your own presets to the pickers.
[*][b]The named people.[/b] 43 companions and major NPCs, 26 women and 17 men, have a body that fits who they are: Piper, Cait, Curie, Magnolia, Preston, Danse, MacCready, Deacon, Maxson and more.
[*][b]Factions[/b] (built, not yet seen in game). Eleven factions draw from ten bodies per sex in their own look: drilled Brotherhood soldiers, underfed raiders, lean Gunners, soft Institute scientists, gaunt Children of Atom. 220 bodies, measured like the pool.
[*][b]Your rules.[/b] OBody NG's own JSON keys and priority: per NPC by form id or name, blacklists, faction, plugin, race. A rule of yours always wins over Silhouette's.
[*][b]Your character[/b] is never randomised. Pick a body in MCM, or keep the pool's most average one.
[/list]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-silhouette@4da5046883246533fd9d015a70e87c1f10e51840/docs/img/factions.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][i]Each faction's bodies, by overall size and belly, women and men. Size is the sum of seven girths.[/i][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-silhouette@4da5046883246533fd9d015a70e87c1f10e51840/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#e8b99c]In game[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Try every body on anyone.[/b] Five hotkeys, unbound until you set them: [i]Pick[/i] the NPC you aim at, [i]Next[/i] and [i]Previous[/i] to try each preset on them live, [i]Keep[/i], or [i]Cancel[/i] back to exactly what they had. The lists have no length limit, past Papyrus's 128-entry cap.
[*][b]The MCM page for the NPC in your sights:[/b] give them a preset from a list, reset them, or ask which body they have.
[*][b]For the people around you:[/b] count the bodies, refresh them with this build's values, or give them new ones. [i]Reset everyone[/i] starts the whole save over.
[*][b]Old saves too.[/b] A save that never had Silhouette gets bodies for everyone on its first load, once, with a notification (seen in game: 39 people on an old save). A switch in MCM turns it off (built, not yet seen in game).
[/list]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-silhouette@4da5046883246533fd9d015a70e87c1f10e51840/docs/img/picker.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-silhouette@4da5046883246533fd9d015a70e87c1f10e51840/docs/img/oldsaves.jpg[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#e8b99c]Clothing: ORefit[/color][/b][/size]

While someone is dressed, their breasts are held together and lifted, and under heavy clothes their nipples are flattened (built, not yet seen in game); a light bodysuit showing her own was seen. Heavy is told by the item's [b]name[/b] (armor, jacket, coat, parka and more, whole words only), not by its slot, and you can name items heavy or light yourself. ORefit only ever raises a slider, under a keyword of its own: the moment they undress they are exactly their own body.

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-silhouette@4da5046883246533fd9d015a70e87c1f10e51840/docs/img/cloth.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][i]Measured over the author's 816-plugin load order: 137 garments flattened under the old slot rule, 35 under the name rule, and no bra, top or shirt among them any more. The bodysuit was seen in game; the coat is flattened by the rule.[/i][/center]

The flattening shows only on outfits whose meshes carry the refit sliders (mod outfits built with them; no vanilla or DLC heavy outfit does).

[size=5][b][color=#e8b99c]Variety, and other mods[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Every person has their own nipples (size, areola, tip, length) and, on the anatomy bodies, their own genital shape. Never a runtime state: scenes own those.
[*][b]AAF-aware:[/b] anyone in a scene waits, and their change lands when the scene ends.
[*]Other mods' morphs under their own keyword are never touched. People another mod marked before Silhouette arrived get a body within a 24-hour window, keeping that mod's morphs.
[*]Works with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109435]Anatomy[/url]: its arousal keeps nipples flat under armour Silhouette marks heavy.
[/list]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-silhouette@4da5046883246533fd9d015a70e87c1f10e51840/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#e8b99c]Install[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]In BodySlide, build your body (CBBE for women, BodyTalk for men) and your outfits from a zeroed preset ("CBBE Zeroed Sliders", "BT - Zero") with [b]Build Morphs[/b] ticked. You do not need to build Silhouette's own presets: the bodies are applied in game.
[*]Install Silhouette with your mod manager and enable [font=Courier New]Silhouette.esp[/font].
[*]Load a save. A save that never had Silhouette gets bodies for everyone by itself, once, with a notification; a new game needs nothing.
[*]Optional: set the picker hotkeys in MCM > Silhouette > The NPC in your sights.
[/list]
No Python and no generator for any of this. [b]For power users:[/b] the generator ([font=Courier New]tools/silhouette_gen.py[/font] on [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-silhouette]GitHub[/url], Python 3) puts your own installed presets in the pickers, compiles your own distribution rules, and handles a body that was not built zeroed.

[quote]
[b]Needs:[/b] Fallout 4 1.10.163 (not next-gen) with F4SE 0.6.23 (the plugin refuses other runtimes), LooksMenu with BodyGen on, MCM, and the Visual C++ 2015-2022 Redistributable 14.40 or newer. Your body and outfits built in BodySlide from a zeroed preset ("CBBE Zeroed Sliders", "BT - Zero") with Build Morphs ticked. [font=Courier New]Silhouette.esp[/font] is a light plugin: no load-order slot.
[/quote]

[size=5][b][color=#e8b99c]FAQ[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Is it tested?[/b]
[spoiler]Offline, with 553 plugin tests and 152 tool tests. Seen in the author's game: the pool and the named bodies, nipples through a light bodysuit, the picker, the fresh start on an old save, touch-ups and refits. Built and tested offline but not yet seen in game: the faction bodies, the heavy-clothes flattening, the MCM switches, and the notifications while another mod's scene holds a change. The in-game checklist is [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-silhouette/blob/master/docs/phase2-test-plan.md]on GitHub[/url]. Please tell us what you see.[/spoiler]

[b]Which game versions?[/b]
[spoiler]Old-gen now: Fallout 4 1.10.163 with F4SE 0.6.23. Next-gen (1.10.984) and the Anniversary builds (1.11.x) are coming through [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url], so one build will run on all three. No date yet.[/spoiler]

[b]Safe to add or remove mid-playthrough?[/b]
[spoiler]Adding: yes. The first load of a save runs Reset everyone once, with a notification; turn "Fresh start for saves new to Silhouette" off in MCM > Silhouette > Settings to keep the bodies you have. Removing: disable Silhouette.esp and remove the files. The bodies stay (they are LooksMenu's data in your save), and the clothed shapes go with the esp. Adding it back to that save later counts as a new save again, so the fresh start runs once more.[/spoiler]

[b]What are its limits?[/b]
[spoiler]ORefit only raises a slider; it cannot lower one, because LooksMenu keeps the highest value per keyword. Heavy clothes are told by English names; a localized game needs its words added to [font=Courier New]heavyWords[/font]. Faction rules read an NPC record's own factions, as OBody does, not its templates'. There is no custom menu, to stay clear of a known plugin-menu crash on 1.10.163: the picker is MCM and hotkeys.[/spoiler]

[b]Where are all the settings, and the API?[/b]
[spoiler]In the sticky posts: every feature, every MCM page and config key, and the API for mod authors with OBody NG's names.[/spoiler]

